# Angular Speech Toolkit Notes 🎤

## Introduction

Angular Speech Toolkit means adding **voice capabilities** to an Angular application.

It allows users to interact with the application using voice commands instead of only using keyboard and mouse.

The two main features are:

1. **Speech Recognition (Voice → Text)**
2. **Text To Speech (Text → Voice)**

---

# 1. Speech Recognition (Voice → Text)

Speech Recognition converts human voice into text.

### Flow:

```
User Voice
     |
     ↓
Microphone
     |
     ↓
Speech Recognition API
     |
     ↓
Text Output
     |
     ↓
Angular Component
```

### Example:

User says:

```
Calculate my insurance premium
```

Speech Recognition converts it into:

```
"Calculate my insurance premium"
```

Now Angular can process this text.

---

# 2. Text To Speech (Text → Voice)

Text To Speech converts application text into human-like voice.

### Flow:

```
Text
 |
 ↓
Speech Synthesis
 |
 ↓
Voice Output
```

### Example:

Application response:

```
Your policy has been approved.
```

Browser speaks:

🔊 Your policy has been approved.

---

# Web Speech API in Angular

Angular can use the browser's built-in Web Speech API.

Main APIs:

### Speech Recognition

```javascript
webkitSpeechRecognition
```

Used for:

- Listening to user voice
- Converting speech into text


### Speech Synthesis

```javascript
speechSynthesis
```

Used for:

- Converting text into audio

---

# Creating Speech Recognition Service

Create service:

```
ng generate service speech
```

File:

```
speech.service.ts
```

Example:

```typescript
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';

@Injectable({
  providedIn:'root'
})
export class SpeechService {

  recognition:any;


  constructor(){

    const SpeechRecognition =
    window.webkitSpeechRecognition;


    this.recognition =
    new SpeechRecognition();


    this.recognition.lang = "en-US";


    this.recognition.continuous = false;

  }


  startListening(callback:any){


    this.recognition.start();


    this.recognition.onresult =
    (event:any)=>{


      const text =
      event.results[0][0].transcript;


      callback(text);

    }

  }

}
```

---

# Using Speech Service in Component

Component:

```typescript
constructor(
 private speechService:SpeechService
){}



startMic(){


 this.speechService
 .startListening((text:string)=>{


   console.log(text);


 });


}
```

HTML:

```html
<button (click)="startMic()">

