# Speech Technologies

## 1. Web Speech API

### Advantages:

- Free
- Easy implementation
- No API key required
- Browser supported


### Limitations:

- Browser dependent
- Chrome provides better support

---

# 2. Google Cloud Speech-To-Text

Used for enterprise-level applications.

Architecture:

```
Angular

↓

Node.js Backend

↓

Google Speech API

↓

Text Response
```

Advantages:

- High accuracy
- Multiple language support
- Cloud processing

---

# 3. Microsoft Azure Speech SDK

Features:

- Real-time speech recognition
- Multiple languages
- High accuracy
- Enterprise support

---

# Angular Speech Best Practices

## 1. Create Separate Speech Service

Do not write speech logic directly inside component.

Good:

```
Component
    |
    ↓
Speech Service
```

---

## 2. Handle Microphone Permission

Always check:

- User allowed microphone
- Browser support
- Permission denied errors

---

## 3. Handle Errors

Examples:

```
No microphone found

Permission denied

Speech not recognized

Network error
```

---

## 4. Stop Recognition Properly

After speech completion:

```typescript
recognition.stop();
```

Avoid:

```
InvalidStateError:
recognition already started
```

---

# Speech Recognition vs Text To Speech

| Speech Recognition | Text To Speech |
|---|---|
| Voice → Text | Text → Voice |
| Takes microphone input | Gives audio output |
| Uses SpeechRecognition API | Uses SpeechSynthesis API |
| Used for commands | Used for assistant replies |

